hadiths[165]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1651","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: We are Affan bin Muslim, and Yahya bin Hammad, and Al-Nasaq is by Affan, he said: We are Abu Awanah, On the authority of Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar Ziyad Ibn Kulayb, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Qarth’ al-Dhabi, on the authority of Salman, he said: The Messenger said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Do you know what Friday is?” I said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: “But I am telling you about Friday.” Friday, a man does not purify himself, then walks to Friday prayer, then listens until the imam finishes his prayer, unless it is expiation for what is in between, and between “The Friday before that he did not avoid the killing.”"
"1652","Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: I am Al-Hussein Al-Ja’fi, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir, on the authority of Abu Al-Ash’ath Al-San’ani, On the authority of Aws ibn Aws, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Indeed, one of the best of your days is Friday, on which Adam was created, and on which he died. And therein is the blast, and therein is the thunderbolt, so increase your blessings upon me therein, for your prayers will be presented to me.” They said: O Messenger of God, and how will you be presented? Our prayers be upon you and you have died? That is, they say, “You have perished.” He said, “Indeed, God has forbidden the earth to consume the bodies of the prophets.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1653","Muhammad bin Salamah Abu Al-Harith Al-Masry told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Harith, that Saeed bin Abi Hilal, And Bukair bin Al-Ashjaj, they told him, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Amr bin Sulaym, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Abi Saeed, on the authority of His father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Ghusling on Friday is obligatory for every pubescent person, and the siwak, and touching on any perfume.” He was destined for him.” However, Bukair did not mention Abdul Rahman, and he said regarding perfume: Even if it is from a woman’s perfume. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1654","Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Safwan bin Sulaym, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yasar, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Ghusl on Friday is obligatory for every pubescent person.”"
"1655","Humayd bin Masada told us, he said: Bishr told us, he said: Dawud told us, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “Every Muslim man must perform ablution every seven days, and that is Friday.”"
"1656","Kathir ibn Ubaid al-Humsi told us, he said: Muhammad ibn Harb al-Humsi told us, on the authority of al-Zubaidi, on the authority of al-Zuhri, he said: Salem informed me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of Omar bin Al-Khattab, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever of you comes on Friday, let him wash himself.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1657","Kathir ibn Ubaid told us, he said: Muhammad told us, and he is Ibn Harb, on the authority of al-Zubaidi, on the authority of al-Zuhri, he said: Salem told me, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Omar, that: He heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever of you comes on Friday, let him wash himself.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1658","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “If “If one of you comes to Friday prayer, let him wash.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1659","Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan Masisi told me, he said: Hajjaj told me, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Shihab told me, on the authority of Salem bin Abd God, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: “Whoever of you comes on Friday, let him wash himself.”"
"1660","Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan told me, he said: Hajjaj bin Muhammad told me, he said: Ibn Jurayj said, Ibn Shihab told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said while he was standing on the pulpit: “Whoever of you comes Friday, let him wash himself.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1661","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said while he was standing on the pulpit: “Whoever of you comes for Friday prayer, let him wash himself.”"
"1662","Ubayd Allah ibn Fadalah informed us, he said: I am Muhammad, he said: Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, he said: Nafi’ informed me, that Ibn Omar told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you comes on Friday, let him wash.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1663","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave a speech He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “If one of you goes to Friday prayers, let him take a bath.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1664","Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When he comes If one of you prays for Friday prayer, let him wash himself.”"
"1665","Hanad bin Al-Sirri told us, on the authority of Abu Bakr, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “Whoever comes to the Friday prayer, let him take a bath.”"
"1666","Amr ibn Ali informed us, he said: Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Yahya ibn Wathhab, he said: I heard Ibn Umar He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever comes to Friday prayer, let him wash himself.”"
"1667","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Abdullah Al-Naysaburi told me, he said: Abu Al-Yaman told us, he said: I am Shuaib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Tawoos said I said to Ibn Abbas: They mentioned that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Bathe yourself, and wash your heads, even if you are not in a state of ritual impurity, and they were Of perfume.” Ibn Abbas said: As for washing, yes, but as for perfume, I do not know. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1668","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid, the Meccan reciter, informed us. He said: My father told us. He said: Saeed told us. He said: Abu Al-Aswad told me, on the authority of Urwa, he said: Aisha said: “The companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, were a people who worked themselves, and they had souls. So it was said to them: If only you had bathed. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1669","Mahmoud bin Khalid told me, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Muslim, he said: Abdullah bin Al-Ala’ told me that he heard Al-Qasim bin Muhammad bin Abi Bakr, that they mentioned performing the ritual ablution on Friday with Aisha, and she said: The people used to live in Al-Aliyah, so they would attend Friday prayers. And they have filth, and when the spirit afflicts them, their souls shine, and people are harmed by them. This was mentioned to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted him and said: “Shall they not take a bath?” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1670","Abu Al-Ash'ath Ahmad ibn Al-Miqdam Al-Ijli told us, on the authority of Yazid, who was Ibn Zurai', he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever performs ablution on Friday will do it, and you will be blessed, and whoever performs ablution, Washing is better.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah in a letter, and Al-Hasan did not hear from Samurah except the hadith about the Aqeeqah, by God. God Almighty knows best"
"1671","Amr bin Mansour and Harun bin Muhammad bin Bakkar bin Bilal told us, and the pronunciation is his. He said: We are Abu Mushar. He said: We are Saeed bin Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Yahya bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Abu Al-Ash’ath Al-San’ani, on the authority of Aws bin Aws, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Whoever washes himself, takes a bath, eats the morning and prays early, approaches the imam, and does not cancel, will have for each step the action of a year, its fasting, and its prayers in prayer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1672","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, that Omar bin Al-Khattab saw Hilla at the door of The mosque, and he said: O Messenger of God, if you bought this and wore it on Friday, and for the delegation when they came to you? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “This will only be worn by one who has no share in the Hereafter.” Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came. He took some of it off, and he gave Omar one of it, and Omar said: O Messenger of God, you clothed me with it, and you said what you said about the suit of Mercury, the Messenger of God said. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “I did not clothe her so that she could wear it, but Omar, a brother of his who was a polytheist in Mecca, clothed her.”"
"1673","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Abdullah bin Al-Harith Al-Makhzoumi, on the authority of Hanzalah bin Abi Sufyan, on the authority of Salem bin Abdul God, he said: I heard Ibn Umar narrating that Umar ibn al-Khattab went out and saw a garment of brocade being sold in the market, so he came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: O Messenger of God, I bought it, so wear it on Friday and when the delegation comes to you. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He, peace and blessings of God be upon him: “Only those who have no manners wear these clothes.” He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came with three garments from them, and they dressed Omar. One of them was a suit, and he covered Ali with a suit, and he covered Osama with a suit, so he came to him and said: O Messenger of God, did you say about it what you said, then you sent it to me? ! He said: “Sell it and fulfill your need with it, or divide it as wine among your wives.”"
"1674","Harun bin Abdullah told me, he said: Al-Hasan bin Suwar told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Al-Munakadir, that Amr bin Sulaym told him, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Sa`id, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He said: “It is obligatory for every pubescent person to wash on Friday, to use the siwak, and to touch as much perfume as he can.”"
"1675","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman bin Dawud told me, he said: Ishaq bin Bakr bin Mudar told me, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, and Abd al-Malik bin Shuaib bin Al-Layth bin Saad told us, he said: My father told me, he said: my grandfather told me, he said: he told me Aqeel, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Hurmuz al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If it was Friday, there would be angels at every door of the mosque, writing the first, then the first. When the imam sat, they folded the pages. And they came to listen to the remembrance.”"
"1676","Muhammad bin Khalid told me, he said: Bishr bin Shuaib informed me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Abu Salamah and Abu Abd informed me. God Almighty, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When it is Friday, it is on every door of In the mosque there are angels who write down the first, then the first, and when the imam sits, they fold the pages, and sit down and listen to the dhikr.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1677","Amr bin Uthman bin Saeed bin Kathir told me, he said: Al-Walid told me, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir, that he: He heard Aba Al-Ash'ath narrates that he heard Aws bin Aws, the companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever performs ablution on Friday, and performs the ritual ablution in the morning, and departs early, and walks, and does not ride, and approaches the imam and listens, and does not cancel, will have “With every step, one year’s work.”"
"1678","Mahmoud bin Khaled told me, he said: Al-Walid told me, he said: Ibn Jabir told me, he said: Abu Al-Ash’ath told me, he said: I heard Aws bin Aws, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Amr bin Uthman told me. He said: Al-Walid told me, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir, That he heard Abu Al-Ash’ath narrating that he heard Aws bin Aws, who was the companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Whoever bathed on Friday, and did so in the morning, and rose early, and walked, and did not ride, approached the imam and listened, And he did not cancel. He had a year’s worth of action for every step.” Mahmoud said in his hadith: “So when the imam came out, he listened and did not cancel, he had a work to do with it.” One year,” Ibn Jabir said: Then Yahya bin Al-Harith reminded me of this, and he said: I heard Abu Al-Ash’ath narrating this hadith, and he said: With every precedence, he performed a year of fasting and standing in prayer.” Ibn Jabir said: Yahya memorized it and I forgot."
"1679","Nasr bin Ali bin Nasr al-Jahdami al-Basri told us, on the authority of Abd al-Ala, he said: Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of al-Aghar Abi Abd God, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “When it is Friday, the angels sit at the doors of the mosque.” So they wrote down whoever came to Friday prayer, and when the imam came out, the angels folded the pages. He said: And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The one who migrates to Friday is like the Mahdi a camel, then like the Mahdi a cow, then like the Mahdi a sheep, then like the Mahdi a duck, then like the Mahdi a chicken, Then the Mahdi is like an egg.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1680","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Al-Zuhri told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he conveyed it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “When it was Friday, there would be angels at every door of the mosque, meaning angels, writing the people to their homes, the first and the first.” When the imam comes out, the newspapers are folded and they listen to the sermon. The one who migrates to prayer is like the Mahdi with a camel, then the one who follows him is like the Mahdi with a cow. Then the next one is like the Mahdi, a ram, until he mentioned the hen and the egg.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1681","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, he said: Shuaib bin Al-Layth told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Sumayy, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Huraira, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “On Friday, angels sit at the gates of the mosque, calling the people to Their homes, the people in it are like a man offering a camel, and like a man offering a camel, and like a man offering a cow, and like a man offering a cow, and like a man offering a sheep, And as a man offered a sheep, and as a man offered a chicken, and as a man offered a chicken, and as a man offered a bird, and as a man offered a bird, and as a man offered an egg “And like a man who has laid an egg.”"
"1682","Mahmoud bin Khaled told me, he said: Al-Walid told us, he said: Ibn Jabir told us, he said: Abu Al-Ash’ath told us, he said: I heard Aws Ibn Aws, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Omar Ibn Uthman told me, saying: Al-Walid told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman Bin Yazid bin Jabir, that he heard Abu Al-Ash’ath, narrating that he heard Aws bin Aws, the companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever takes a bath on Friday and washes himself, and wakes up early in the morning, and walks but does not ride, and approaches the imam, And he listened and did not cancel. He had a year of action for every step he took.” Mahmoud said in his hadith: “So when the imam came out, he listened and did not cancel. He has one year to do with it.” Ibn Jabir said: Then Yahya bin Al-Harith reminded me of this, and he said: I heard Abu Al-Ash’ath narrating this hadith. And he said: “With every beginning he performed a sunnah: fasting and standing in prayer.” Ibn Jabir said: Yahya memorized it and I forgot."
"1683","Qutayba bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Sumayy, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: “Whoever takes a bath on Friday has done the ritual bath of ritual impurity, and goes, it is as if he has offered a camel sacrifice, and whoever goes in the second hour, it is as if he has offered the sacrifice.” A cow, and whoever goes at the third hour, it is as if he has sacrificed a ram, and whoever goes at the fourth hour, it is as if he has sacrificed a hen, and whoever goes At five o’clock, it is as if he had offered an egg, and when the imam came out, the angels were present, listening to the remembrance.”"
"1684","Amr ibn Sawad ibn al-Aswad ibn Amr and al-Harith ibn Miskin informed us of a reading to him, and I am listening, and the pronunciation is his, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Al-Jalah, the client of Abdul-Aziz, that Abu Salamah bin Abdul-Rahman told him, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “On Friday there are twelve hours in which there is an hour when no servant is found.” “A Muslim asks God for something but He gives it to him, so seek it in the last hour after the afternoon prayer.”"
"1685","Shuaib bin Yusuf al-Nasa’i told me, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told me, on the authority of Ali bin al-Harith, he said: I heard Iyas bin Salamah bin Al-Akwa’, narrating: On the authority of his father, he said: “We used to pray Friday prayers with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and then we would return, and the walls had no shelter.” He will be shaded by it.”"
"1686","Harun bin Abdullah told me, he said: Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Hassan bin Ayyash told us, he said: Jafar bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Jabir, he said: “We used to pray Friday prayers with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and then we would come back and rest our sandals. I said: What time is it?” He said. : “zenith” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1687","Muhammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Al-Sa’ib bin Yazid informed me: “That The call to prayer was the first time when the imam sat on the pulpit on Friday, during the era of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Bakr and Omar. When the caliphate of Uthman came, and the people were many, Uthman ibn Affan ordered the third call to prayer on Friday, so he announced it to the Zawra’, and the matter was confirmed. On that \ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"1688","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Al-Mu`tamir told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Al-Sa’ib bin Yazid, he said: “Bilal used to give the call to prayer When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sat on the pulpit on Friday, and when he came down, he remained standing. Then this was the case in the time of Abu Bakr. \And Omar\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"1689","Muhammad ibn Yahya informed us, he said: Ya’qub told us, he said: Ubayy told us, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that Al-Sa’ib ibn Yazid informed him: “ Uthman only ordered the third call to prayer when the people of Medina were large, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had only one call to prayer, so it was The call to prayer on Friday when the imam is seated.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1690","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khalid told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, he said: I heard Jabir bin Abdullah, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you comes and the imam has left, let him pray two rak’ahs.” Shu’bah said: On Friday. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1691","Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan Al-Masisi and Yusuf bin Saeed Al-Masisi told me, and the pronunciation is his, he said: Na Hajjaj, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, he said: Amr bin Dinar told me that he heard Jabir bin Abdullah say: A man came while the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was on the pulpit on the day of Friday, so he said to him: “Did you kneel two rak’ahs?” He said: No, he said: “Kneel.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1692","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: Salik Al-Ghatfani came, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, was sitting on the pulpit, then Salik sat down before praying, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Did you kneel two rak’ahs?”, he said. No, he said: “Get up and kneel on them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1693","Wahb bin Bayan Al-Masry told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: I heard Muawiyah, speaking, on the authority of Abu Al-Zahiriyah, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Busr said: I was sitting next to him on Friday. He said: A man came to jump around people’s necks on Friday, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace. He was addressing the people, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Sit down, for you have been offended.”"
"1694","Mahmoud bin Khalid told me, he said: Our name is Omar, meaning Ibn Abd al-Wahid, he said: I heard Yahya bin Al-Harith, speaking, on the authority of Abu Al-Ash’ath Al-San’ani, on the authority of Aws bin Aws Al-Thaqafi, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “Whoever washes and takes a bath, then goes out early in the morning and approaches From the imam and he listened, then he did not cancel. He had for every step the reward of a year of fasting and praying prayers.”"
"1695","Abdul Rahman bin Muhammad told us, he said: Amr bin Muhammad told us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Issa, on the authority of Yahya bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Abu Al-Ash’ath, on the authority of Aws ibn Aws, who said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever washes and takes a bath, then the next day He took the initiative and sat close to the imam, so he listened and listened. For every step he took, he would receive the reward of a year of fasting and praying in prayer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1696","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna and Muhammad bin Bashar informed us, saying: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: I heard Abu Ishaq, speaking, on the authority of my father Ubaida, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: He taught us the sermon to the needy: “Praise be to God. We seek His help and seek His forgiveness. We seek refuge in God from the evils of our own selves. Whoever God guides, none can mislead him, and whoever He leads astray, none can guide him. I bear witness that there is no god but God, and I bear witness that there is no god but God. Indeed, Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger. Then three verses will be recited: O you who have believed, fear God as He should be feared, and do not die except as Muslims. O people, fear your Lord, who created you from one soul and created from it its mate and dispersed from them many men and women. Those who believe fear God and speak words of righteousness. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1697","Amr bin Sawad bin Al-Aswad bin Amr told us, he said: I am Abdullah bin Wahb, he said: I am Ibn Jurayj, that Abu Al-Zubayr, He told him that he heard Jabir bin Abdullah say: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to: “When he delivered a sermon, he would lean on the trunk of a palm tree. The poles of the mosque. When the pulpit was made for it and it was mounted on it, that pole stirred like the longing of a camel, until the people of the mosque heard it. Until the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came down to her and embraced her, and she remained calm.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1698","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Bishr bin al-Mufaddal told us, he said: Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Abdullah, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “He would deliver two sermons while standing, and he would separate them by sitting.”"
"1699","Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Al-Hakam told us, he said: Muhammad bin Jafar told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, On the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Ka’b ibn Ujrah, he said: He entered the mosque and Abd al-Rahman ibn Umm al-Hakam was giving the sermon while sitting, so he said: “Look at This man is delivering a speech while sitting, and God, Blessed and Most High, said: And when they see commerce or amusement, they rush to it and leave you standing. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1700","Muhammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Nashit, that he asked Ibn Shihab, “about washing on Friday.” He said: It is a Sunnah, and Salem told me, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, spoke about it on the pulpit. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1701","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Husayn bin Abdul Rahman, he said: I saw Bishr bin Marwan, on the authority of Friday, he raised his hands, and Amara bin Ruwaybah said: May God bless these hands. I have seen the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, more than And he pointed with his index finger."
"1702","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Waki’ told us, Sufyan said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Husayn, that Bishr bin Marwan raised his hands on Friday to On the pulpit, and Amara bin Ruwaybah Al-Thaqafi insulted him and said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not add anything more to this, and he pointed with his finger. \index finger\"""""""
"1703","Muhammad bin Abdul Aziz bin Abi Rizmah informed us, saying: I am Al-Fadl bin Musa, on the authority of Al-Hussein bin Waqid, he said: Yahya bin told me Aqeel said: I heard Abdullah bin Abi Awfa saying: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to talk a lot, talk less and talk for a long time.” Prayer, shortening the sermon, and not refraining from walking with the widow and the poor and fulfilling their needs.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1704","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, told us He was delivering the Friday sermon, when a man came and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Did you pray?” He said: No. He said: “Get up and kneel.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1705","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: I am Abu Musa, he said: I heard Al-Hasan, saying: I heard Abu Bakra, saying: I have I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the pulpit, and Al-Hassan was with him, and he was approaching the people once, and once towards him, and saying: “This is my son.” Master, and perhaps God will bring about great reconciliation through him between two groups of Muslims.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1706","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Ibn Ajlan told us, on the authority of Iyad bin Abdullah, he said: I heard Aba Saeed, saying: A man came on Friday while the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was giving the sermon in a splendid appearance, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: He said: “Did you pray?” He said: “No.” He said: “Pray two rak’ahs.” Then he urged the people to give charity. They threw some clothes, and they gave him two of them. When It was the second Friday. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came and delivered a sermon and urged the people to give charity. Then one of his clothes was thrown on, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: “He came on Friday looking beautiful, so I ordered the people to give charity, so they threw away clothes, so I ordered him to give him two of them. Then he came now, so I ordered the people to give charity, and one of them met him and rebuked him and said: Take your dress.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1707","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us, he said: Harun ibn Ismail informed us, he said: Ali ibn al-Mubarak informed us, he said: Yahya informed us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Abd Al-Rahman, on the authority of the daughter of Harithah bin Al-Nu’man, who said: “I memorized Q and the Glorious Qur’an from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he is on The pulpit on Friday.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1708","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Abdul Razzaq, he said: we are Muammar, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: “it was The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, delivers the sermon twice on Friday, with a session between them.”"
"1709","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Bishr bin al-Mufaddal told us, he said: Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Abdullah, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “He would deliver two sermons while standing, and he would separate them by sitting.”"
"1710","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Bazi’ told us, he said: we are Yazid, meaning Ibn Zurai’, he said: we are Israel, he said: we are Samak, on the authority of Jabir bin Samra, he said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “delivering the sermon on Friday standing, then sitting down and not speaking, then getting up and giving the sermon.” Another sermon. Whoever tells you that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, delivered a sermon sitting has lied.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1711","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Jarir, on the authority of Mansour bin Al-Mu’tamir Al-Sulami, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar Ziyad bin Kulayb, on the authority of Ibrahim On the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Al-Qartha’ Al-Dhabi, who was one of the first reciters, on the authority of Salman, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: “There is no A man purifies himself on Friday as he was commanded, then leaves his house until Friday comes, and remains silent until he completes his prayer, unless it is an expiation. Because it was Friday before that.”"
"1712","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: We are Affan bin Muslim, and Yahya bin Hammad, and Al-Nasaq is for Affan, he said: I am Abu Awanah, on the authority of Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Qarth’ al-Dhabi, on the authority of Salman, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “Do you know what Friday is?” I said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: “But I am telling you about Friday, one does not purify oneself.” A man then walks to the Friday prayer and then listens until the imam finishes his prayer, unless it is an expiation for what happened between them and the Friday prayer that was before it. \You avoided the murderer.\"""""""
"1713","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: I am Yahya, he said: Malik told us, he said: Al-Zuhri told me, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “If a man says to his companion on Friday while the imam is giving the sermon: Listen, then he has negligently done so.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1714","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Aqeel, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Whoever says to his companion on Friday while the imam is delivering the sermon: ‘Listen,’ has negligently done so.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1715","Abd Al-Malik bin Shuaib bin Al-Layth bin Saad told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of my grandfather, he said: Aqeel told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, On the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ibrahim bin Qarith, and on the authority of Ibn al-Musayyab, that they told him that Abu Hurairah, He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “If you say to your friend on Friday while the imam is giving the sermon: Listen, then you have gone astray.”"
"1716","Musa bin Abdul-Rahman al-Kufi told us, he said: Husayn bin Ali al-Jufi’i told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir, on the authority of Abu Al-Ash’ath al-San’ani, on the authority of Aws bin Aws, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, and mentioned the Friday prayer: “Whoever washes and takes a bath in the morning, “And he was creative and heeded and did not cancel. He had for every step the reward of a year of fasting and prayer.”"
"1717","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: I am a partner, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Jabir bin Samra, he said: I sat with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, but I did not see him. He delivers the sermon unless he is standing, then he sits, then he stands and delivers the final sermon.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1718","Muhammad bin Abdul Aziz told us, he said: Al-Fadl bin Musa told us, on the authority of Hussein bin Waqid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father He said: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was giving a sermon, when Al-Hasan and Al-Hussein came, wearing red shirts, and they were tripping, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came down.” He, peace and blessings be upon him, interrupted his speech, carried them, then returned to the pulpit, then said: “God has spoken the truth. Your wealth and your children are a test. I saw These two stumbled in their shirts, so I could not wait until I had interrupted my speech and picked them up.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1719","Muhammad bin Ali bin Maimun told me, he said: Al-Faryabi told me, he said: Jarir bin Hazim told me, on the authority of Thabit Al-Bunani, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, He said: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, would come down from the pulpit, and a man would appear to him and speak to him, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, would stand up with him.” Until he fulfills his need, then he goes forward to his place of prayer and prays.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1720","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: I am a partner, on the authority of Zubaid, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Laila, he said: Omar said: “The Friday prayer is two rak’ahs.” And the Fitr prayer is two rak’ahs, and the Al-Adha prayer is two rak’ahs, and the traveling prayer is two rak’ahs, complete and not shortened, according to the tongue of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1721","Ibrahim bin Muhammad told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: Zubaid told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Laila, he said: Omar said: “The traveler’s prayer is two rak’ahs, the Eid al-Adha prayer is two rak’ahs, the Fitr prayer is two rak’ahs, and the Friday prayer is two rak’ahs, complete, and not shortened according to the tongue.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1722","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: Ja`far told us, he said: Ubayy told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abi Rafi’, he said: It was Marwan appoints Abu Hurairah as his successor in charge of Medina, and on Friday Surat Al-Jumu’ah and the Hypocrites will be recited. I said: O Abu Hurairah, I have recited two surahs that Ali used to recite. He said: I heard my beloved Abu al-Qasim, may God bless him and grant him peace, reciting them.”"
"1723","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told me, he said: Khalid bin Al-Harith told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: An authorized person told me, he said: I heard Muslim Al-Bateen, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He used to recite on Friday morning prayers... Download Surat Al-Jumu'ah and the Hypocrites and the Hypocrites in the Friday Prayer. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1724","Qutayba bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Damra bin Saeed, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, that Al-Dahhak bin Qais asked Al-Numan bin Bashir, what did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, use to recite on Friday following Surat Al-Jumu’ah? He said: He used to recite Have you ever heard of the story of cheating?"
"1725","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Al-Muntashir, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Habib bin Salem On the authority of Al-Numan bin Bashir, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “It was recited on the two Eids and on Friday, ‘Glorify the name of your Lord. The highest, and has the hadith about the cheater come to you? Perhaps they came together in one day, and it was recited over them. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1726","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: We are Khaled, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I am Ma’abad bin Khalid, on the authority of Zaid, who is Ibn Uqba, on the authority of Samura, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite on Friday prayers: ‘Glorify the name of your Lord Most High.’ Has the hadith of the deceit reached you?” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1727","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khalid, on the authority of Shu’bah, that Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin al-Muntashir informed him, he said: I heard my father, speaking, on the authority of Habib bin Salim, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Bashir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite in Friday B: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High. Has the hadith of cheating reached you? Perhaps the Eid and the Friday were combined, so it is recited over them all together. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1728","Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who narrates it. He said: “Who has realized who? One rak'ah prayer, and he has reached"
"1729","Abdullah bin Abdul-Samad Musili informed me, he said: Issa bin Yunus, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, and Muhammad bin al-Muthanna informed us, he said: Abd Al-Wahhab, he said: We are servants of God, and the pronunciation is his, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: “Whoever performs one rak’ah of prayer has performed the entire prayer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1730","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “If one of you prays Friday prayers, let him pray four times after it.”"
"1731","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told me, he said: I am Sufyan, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of his father: “The Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: He used to pray two rak’ahs after Friday prayers."
"1732","Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He was not praying after Friday until he finishes, and prays two rak’ahs.”"
"1733","Qutaibah bin Sa’id told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar that: “When he prayed the Friday prayer, he would go away and pray I prostrated two times in his house, then he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to do that.”"
"1734","Abdah bin Abdullah told us, on the authority of Yazid, he said: I am Shu’bah, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar: “He used to pray After the Friday prayer, he performs two rak’ahs in which he prolongs them, and says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to do that.”"
"1735","Qutayba bin Sa`id informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He mentioned Friday, and said: “There is an hour in which no Muslim servant comes, and he is praying, asking God for something, unless He gives it to him,” and indicated The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used his hand to reduce it.”"
"1736","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Abdullah told me, he said: Ahmad bin Hanbal told me, he said: I am Ibrahim bin Khalid, on the authority of Rabah, on the authority of Muammar, On the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab told me, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Indeed, on Friday there is an hour No Muslim servant who asks God for anything agrees with it unless He gives it to him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1737","Amr ibn Zurarah al-Naysaburi told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: Abu al-Qasim said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Indeed, there is an hour on Friday when a Muslim servant, standing and praying, asks God Almighty for something but He gives it to him.” And he said: With his hand. We said: He reduces it and removes it. Amr bin Zurarah told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah: similar to the hadith of Ayyub. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1738","Shuaib bin Yusuf told me, he said: Yazid, he said: I am Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “Indeed, there is an hour on Friday when a Muslim man is standing and praying, asking God for good, but He gives it to him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1739","Al-Fadl bin Sahl told me, he said: Al-Ahwas bin Jawab told me, he said: Ammar bin Ruzaiq told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Ka’b and Abu Hurairah gathered, and Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, on Friday there is an hour when no A Muslim agrees with her in a prayer in which he asks God for good, unless He gives it to him.”"
"1740","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: We are Bakr, and he is Ibn Mudar, on the authority of Ibn al-Hadi, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: I came to Al-Tur, and then I found Ka’b, so he and I stayed for a day telling him about the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, and he was talking to me about the Torah, so I said to him: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The best day on which the sun rises is the day Friday: On it Adam was created, on it he was descended, on it he was repented of, and on it he was taken away, and on it the Hour will come. There is not a living creature on the earth but it will become On Friday, there is an hour that no believer will encounter, and he is in prayer asking God. Nothing except that he gave it to him. Ka’b said: That is a day in every year. I said: Rather, it is every Friday. So Ka’b recited, then said: The Messenger has spoken the truth. May God bless him and grant him peace, it is every Friday.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1741","So I went out and met Basra bin Abi Basra Al-Ghafari, and he said: Where did you come from? I said: From al-Tur. He said: If I had met you before you had come to him, you would not have come to him. I said to him: Why? He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Do not go to the Sacred Mosque except to three mosques: the Sacred Mosque, and my mosque. And the Mosque of Jerusalem.”"
"1742","So I met Abdullah bin Salam, and I said to him: If you had seen me, I went out to Al-Tur and met Ka’b. He and I stayed for a day telling him about the Messenger of God. God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he was talking to me about the Torah, so I said to him: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The best day is on which the sun rises.” Friday is the day on which Adam was created, and on it he was descended, and on it he was repented of, and on it he was taken away, and on it the Hour will come. There is not a living creature on the earth except it. On Friday morning there is an hour until the sun rises, the twilight of the Hour, except for the son of Adam, and there is an Hour that no believing servant will encounter, and he is in Prayer: He asks God for something but He gives it to him.” Ka’b said: That is a day every year. Abdullah bin Salam said: Ka’b lied. I said: Then Ka'b read and said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, spoke the truth, and it was every Friday. Abdullah bin Salam said: Ka'b spoke the truth, I know. That hour, I said: O brother, tell me about it. He said: It is the last hour of Friday before the sun sets, so I said: Isn’t it? Did you hear the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “No believer will meet her while he is in prayer”? And that hour is not a prayer. He said: Have you not heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Whoever prays and sits waiting for the prayer, will not stop praying.” Until the prayer that follows it comes?” I said: “Yes.” He said: “It is like that.”"
"1743","Abu Abd al-Rahman told us, he said: I am Ali bin Hajar, he said: Ismail told us, he said: Humaid told me, on the authority of Anas, he said: It was for the people of In pre-Islamic times there were two days every year on which they played. When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to Medina, he said: “You had two days to play.” “And God has given you in exchange for them better than them: the Day of Breakfast and the Day of Sacrifice.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1744","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, he said: Abu Bishr told me, on the authority of Abu Umair bin Anas, on the authority of Ummah To him, that a people saw the crescent, so they came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He ordered them to break their fast after the day had risen, and to They will go out to the Eid the next day.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1745","Amr bin Zurarah told us, he said: I am Ismail, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Hafsa, she said: Umm Atiyya did not remember the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. She, peace and blessings of God be upon him, never said: May my father be sacrificed. I said: Did you hear the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “So-and-so?” She said: Yes. By Aba, he said: “Let the freed women, the virgins, and the menstruating women come out and witness goodness, and the call of the Muslims, and keep away from the menstruating women.” The prayer hall"
"1746","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: I am Sufyan, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: I met Umm Atiya, and I said to her: Have you heard from The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace? And whenever she mentioned him, she would say: “By Aba.” She said: “By Aba.” He said: “Bring out the freedmen and the young women, so that they may bear witness.” Eid, and the invitation to Muslims, and the menstruating woman should withdraw from the people’s prayer place.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1747","Ahmad bin Ali told us, he said: Suraij told us, he said: Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Umm Atiyya, and Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, and Hafsa, on the authority of Umm Atiyya, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He used to bring out the virgins and the freed women with maidens. And the menstruating woman during the two Eids. As for the menstruating women, they should isolate themselves from the prayer place, witness goodness, and invite the Muslims. One of them said: If not Does one of us have a jilbab? He said: “Let her sister strip her of her jilbab.”"
"1748","Ahmad ibn Amr ibn al-Sarh and Sulayman ibn Dawud informed us, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, who said: Yunus ibn Yazid and Amr ibn Al-Harith, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Salim bin Abdullah, on the authority of his father, who said: “Umar bin Al-Khattab found a suit of Istabraq being sold in the market So he took it and brought it to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, buy this and decorate yourself with it for the Eid. And to the delegation, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “This is the clothing of one who has no manners, or this is only worn by one who has no manners.” Omar stayed for as long as God willing, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent to him with a brocade robe, and he accepted it until he brought it to the Messenger of God. God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: O Messenger of God, you said: This is the clothing of one who has no manners. Then you sent this to me, and he said? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Sell it and meet your need with it.” The wording is from Solomon."
"1749","Ishaq bin Mansour informed us, he said: I am Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Aswad ibn Hilal, on the authority of Thalabah ibn It is noteworthy that Ali appointed Abu Masoud as his successor over the people, so he went out on the day of Eid and said: “O people, it is not from the Sunnah to pray before \Imam\"""""""
"1750","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Abi Suleiman, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir bin Abd God said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, led us in prayer on the day of Eid, before the sermon, without the call to prayer or iqamah.”"
"1751","Al-Hasan bin Qazah told us, he said: I am Husayn bin Numayr, on the authority of Al-Fadl bin Atiya, he said: I am Salim bin Abdullah, on the authority of his father, He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out on the day of Eid and prayed without the call to prayer or iqamah.”"
"1752","Muhammad ibn Uthman told us, he said: Bahz, he said: Shu`bah, he said: Zubaid told me, he said: I heard al-Sha`bi, saying: Al-Baraa. Ibn Aazib, at one of the pillars of the mosque, said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, delivered a speech on the Day of Sacrifice, and he said: “The first thing we start with is With it on this day we pray, then we slaughter. Whoever does that has followed our Sunnah, and whoever slaughtered before that is just... Meat to offer to his family.” He said: Abu Burdah ibn Nayyar had slaughtered it before that, and he said: O Messenger of God, I have a log that is better than An elderly woman, and he said: “Slaughter her, and she will not be reimbursed for anyone after you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1753","On the authority of Othman bin Abdullah, on the authority of Affan, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mansour, Daoud, Ibn Aoun, Zubaid, and Mujalid, five of them. On the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, addressed us and said: “The first thing we begin with on this day is to We pray, then we return and slaughter. Whoever does this has followed our Sunnah, and whoever slaughtered before that, it was meat that he offered to his family and was not Of ritual rituals in any way.” He said: And my uncle Abu Burdah ibn Niyar slaughtered. He said: O Messenger of God, I slaughtered while I had a judah that was better than a sharp one. He said: “ Leave it in its place and it will not suffice, or make full payment, on behalf of anyone after you.”"
"1754","Al-Hasan bin Qazah told us, he said: I am Husayn bin Numayr, on the authority of Husayn bin Abdul Rahman, he said: Ata’ told me, on the authority of Jabir, he said: “ The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out on the day of Eid, began, prayed, and then delivered a sermon.”"
"1755","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: I heard Ayoub telling about Ata’, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas saying: “I bear witness I witnessed the Eid with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he began to pray before the sermon, then he delivered a sermon, but he saw that he was not heard. The women, so he came to the women, and he advised them, and reminded them, and commanded them to give charity, and with him was Bilal, who said in his dress like this, that is, he conquered him, so she made “The woman throws the ring, the ring, and the other thing.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1756","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Abdah bin Sulaiman, he said: Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace, Abu Bakr, and Omar: “They would pray the two Eids before the sermon.”"
"1757","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, he said: Al-Hassan bin Muslim told us, on the authority of Tawoos, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: “I witnessed the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Bakr and Omar praying the two Eids before the sermon.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1758","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Abdul Razzaq, he said: I am Muammar, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace: “He used to bring out the goat on the Day of Fitr and on the Day of Eid al-Adha, and he would set it aside and pray over it.”"
"1759","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Sulayman bin Bilal told me, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Anas, He said: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, praying to her in the prayer place.”"
"1760","Imran bin Musa told us, he said: I am Yazid bin Zuray’, he said: I am Sufyan bin Saeed, on the authority of Zubaid al-Ayami, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla mentioned it, on the authority of Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, who said: “The Edha prayer is two rak’ahs, the Fitr prayer is two rak’ahs, the traveler’s prayer is two rak’ahs, and the “Friday is two rak’ahs, complete and not shortened, according to the words of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1761","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Dawud bin Qais told me, he said: Iyad told me, on the authority of Abu Saeed, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “He would go out on the day of Eid and pray two rak’ahs, then give a sermon, and order charity to be given, and he would be the one who gave most of the charity.” Women, if he has a need or wants to send a mission, he will speak, otherwise he will return.”"
"1762","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Damrah bin Saeed told me, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, he said: Omar came out On the day of Eid, Abu Waqid Al-Laythi asked what the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was reciting on this day? He said: By Q. And she approached (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1763","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: We are Waki’, he said: We are Mas’ar, and Sufyan, on the authority of Ma’abad bin Khalid, on the authority of Zayd bin Uqba, on the authority of Samurah ibn Jundub, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “In the two Eids, he used to recite: Glorify the name of your Lord Most High, and has any hadith reached you? Al-Ghashiya"
"1764","Muhammad ibn Qudamah told me, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir. I said: On the authority of his father. He said: Yes, on the authority of Habib ibn Salem, on the authority of Al-Numan bin Bashir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite on Friday and Eid: “Glorify the name of your Lord.” The highest, and has the hadith of cheating reached you? If Friday and Eid come together on the same day, recite them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1765","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Abbas told me, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas, A man said to him: Did you witness the going out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: “Yes, and had I not been in my position I would not have witnessed it, meaning from his childhood. He came to the flag that was at the house of Kathir ibn al-Salt, prayed, then delivered the sermon.” Then he came to the women and admonished them, reminded them, and commanded them to give alms. The woman made her hand go down to, meaning, her throat, throwing In Bilal’s dress, then he and Bilal came home.”"
"1766","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, addressed us. May God bless him and grant him peace: “The Day of Sacrifice after the prayer.”"
"1767","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: I heard Ayoub telling about Ata’, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas saying: “I bear witness “I witnessed the Eid with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he started with prayer before the sermon and then he delivered the sermon.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1768","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Ayyub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Al-Fadl bin Musa told us, he said: I am Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Al-Sa'ib: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed the Eid, and said: “Whoever likes to leave, let him leave, and whoever likes to stay for the sermon, let him stand up.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1769","Muhammad bin Salamah and Al-Harith bin Miskin told us, by reading it, and the pronunciation is his, on the authority of Ibn Al-Qasim, he said: Malik told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If you say to your companion and the imam He preaches: “Listen, for you have gone astray.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1770","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman told us, he said: Ubayd Allah bin Iyad told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Rimtha, he said: “ I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, giving the sermon, wearing two green robes.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1771","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Ibn Abi Zaida told us, he said: Ismail bin Abi Khaled told me, on the authority of his brother, on the authority of Abi Kahil. Al-Ahmasi said: “I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, giving a sermon to a she-camel, and an Ethiopian was holding the camel’s reins.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1772","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Samak, he said: I asked Jabir: Was the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, And he gave the sermon while standing? He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to deliver the sermon standing, then sit down, then stand up."
"1773","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: Abdul Malik bin Abi Suleiman told us, he said: Ataa told us, on the authority of Jabir, he said: I witnessed prayer with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of Eid. He began to pray before the sermon, without the call to prayer or iqamah. When He completed the prayer, stood up, leaning on Bilal, thanked God, praised Him, admonished the people, reminded them, and urged them to obey him, then he went on. To the women, with Bilal with him. He commanded them to fear God, and exhorted them, and reminded them, and praised God, and praised Him, then urged them to She obeyed him, then he said: “Give alms, for the most of you is the firewood of Hell.” Then one of the lowly women with blond cheeks said: Why, oh? Messenger of God? He said: “Because you complained so much and treated your spouse as ungrateful, they began to remove their jewelry, their necklaces, earrings, and rings; they threw them into the “Bilal’s dress that they give in charity.”"
"1774","Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, saying: It was narrated by Abd al-Aziz, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Iyad bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Saeed al-Khudri: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to go out on the Day of Fitr and on the Day of Eid al-Adha to the prayer place, and lead the people in prayer. When he sat down on the second day, He greeted the people, stood up and faced the people, while the people were sitting, if he had a need. He wanted to send a message to the people, otherwise he would order the people to give charity. He said: “Give in charity, give in charity, three times, and he was one of the most “Women give in charity”"
"1775","Utbah bin Abdullah told us, he said: I am Ibn al-Mubarak, he said: I am Sufyan, on the authority of Ja`far bin Muhammad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir, he said : The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say in his sermon: He praises God and praises Him for what He deserves, then he says: “Whoever God guides, none can mislead him, and whoever He leads astray, none can guide him. The most truthful hadith is the Book of God, the best guidance is the guidance of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the worst of matters are newly invented matters, and every newly invented matter is an innovation. And every heresy is a misguidance, and every misguidance is in the Fire. Then he says: “I and the Hour were sent like these.” And when he mentioned the Hour, it turned red. His cheeks rose, his voice rose, and his anger intensified. As if he were the warden of an army. Good morning, may God bless you. Then he said: Whoever leaves behind wealth, it goes to its owner, and whoever leaves behind debt or loss, it goes to me or against me. And I am the guardian of the believers.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1776","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Sammak, on the authority of Jabir bin Samra, he said: “I was praying with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, so his prayer was intentional, and his engagement was intentional.”"
"1777","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Jabir bin Samra, he said: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said the salutation while standing, then he sat for a while without speaking, then he got up and delivered another sermon. “Whoever told you that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, He spoke while sitting, so do not believe him (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1778","Amr bin Ali and Muhammad bin Bashar told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman, who said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Jabir bin Samra, who said: “ The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to deliver the sermon standing, then sit, then stand, recite verses, and remember God, and his sermon was intentionally, and his prayer intentionally.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1779","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abu Tamailah, on the authority of Al-Hussein bin Waqid, on the authority of Ibn Buraydah, on the authority of his father, he said: “Between us The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was on the pulpit giving a sermon, when Hassan and Hussein came, wearing red shirts, walking. And they stumbled, so he came down and picked them up and said: “God has spoken the truth. Your wealth and your children are a trial. Indeed, I saw these two walking and stumbling. I could not wait until I got down, so I carried them.”"
"1780","Muhammad bin Abdul Aziz bin Abi Rizmah told us, he said: I am Al-Fadl bin Musa, on the authority of Hussein bin Waqid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah On the authority of his father, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was giving a sermon, then Al-Hasan and Al-Hussein came, wearing red shirts, and they stumbled over each other. Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came down, stopped his speech, carried them, then returned to the pulpit, and then said: “God has spoken the truth, but your wealth is And your children are a trial. I saw these two stumbling in their shirts, so I could not be patient until I stopped speaking, so I picked them up.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1781","Abdullah bin Saeed told us, he said: Ibn Idris, he said: I am Shu’bah, on the authority of Uday, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He went out on the day of Eid and prayed two rak’ahs. He did not pray before or after them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1782","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Iyas bin Abi Ramla. He said: I heard Muawiyah. Zaid bin Arqam asked: Did you witness two Eids with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: “Yes, he prayed the Eid prayer from the beginning of the day, then made a concession on Friday.”"
"1783","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Abd al-Hamid bin Jaafar told us, he said: Wahb bin Kaysan told me, he said: Aidan during the reign of Ibn al-Zubayr, so he delayed going out until daylight came, then he went out and delivered a sermon, and he prolonged the sermon, then he came down and prayed. He prayed two rak'ahs, and he did not lead the people in Friday prayer on that day. This was mentioned to Ibn Abbas, and he said: He is correct in the Sunnah. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1784","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, he said: Muhammad bin Jafar, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He entered upon her and there were two maidservants beating tambourines. Abu Bakr rebuked them, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “ Leave them, for every people has a festival.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1785","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Ammar told me, he said: I am Al-Mu’affa, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, that Abu Bakr entered upon her, and two maids were with her during the days of Mina, singing; They beat two tambourines while the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was wrapped in his garment. Then Abu Bakr rebuked them, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, revealed Peace be upon him, and he said: “Leave them, Abu Bakr, for these are the days of Eid.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1786","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Isa bin Yunus, he said: I am Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, that Abu A virgin, he entered her during the days of Mina, and there were two maidservants singing and playing tambourines, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was lying on He faced the garment, neither commanding them nor forbidding them. So Abu Bakr rebuked them, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Leave them, O Abu Bakr, for these are the days of Eid.”"
"1787","Muhammad ibn Adam told us, on the authority of Abda, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The Sudanese came to play before the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of Eid, he invited me, and I was looking at them from above him, and I continued to look at him until I was the one who left. \ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"1788","Ishaq bin Musa told us, he said: I am Al-Walid bin Muslim, he said: Al-Awza’i told us, he said: Al-Zuhri told me, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: Omar entered and the Abyssinians were playing in the mosque, and Omar rebuked them, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Leave them, O Omar, for it is only That is, they are the Banu Arfidah."
"1789","Ali bin Khashram told us, he said: I am Isa, he is bin Yunus, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “ I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, covering me with his robe, and I was looking at the Abyssinians playing in the mosque, until I became bored. Appreciate the value of a young girl who is keen on having fun.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1790","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Dawud bin Qais told me, he said: Iyad told me, on the authority of Abu Saeed, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “He would go out on the day of Eid and pray two rak’ahs, then give a sermon, and order charity to be given, and he would be the one who gave most of the charity.” Women, if he has a need or wants to send a mission, he will speak, otherwise he will return.”"
"1791","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Yazid, he said: I am Praiseworthy, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that Ibn Abbas delivered a speech in Basra, and he said: “Give zakat Your fasting. Then he made the people look at one another and said: Who is here from the people of Medina? Go to your brothers and teach them. For they do not know that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, imposed Zakat al-Fitr on the young, the old, the free, and the slave. For the male and the female, half a saa’ of wheat or a saa’ of dates or barley.”"
"1792","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, addressed us. May God bless him and grant him peace, on the Day of Sacrifice after the prayer, then he said: “Whoever prays our prayers and performs our rituals, has performed the rituals, and whoever performs rituals before prayer That is a sheep of meat.” Abu Burdah said: O Messenger of God, by God, we were silent before we went out to pray. I knew that today was the day He ate and drank, so I was in a hurry, ate, and fed my family and neighbors, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, “That is a sheep of meat.” He said: “I have a young she-camel that is better than two lambs, so will that be sufficient for me?” He said: Yes, and it will not be sufficient for anyone after you."
"1793","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Al-Mu`tamir told us, he said: Abdullah bin Al-Taifi told us, he said: Amr bin Shuaib, he said: My father told me, that Amr ibn Al-Aas, narrated on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The takbeer for breaking the fast is seven in the first. And the last five.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1794","I am Qutayba bin Saeed, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Sharik bin Abdullah bin Abi Nimr, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, who said: A man came to the Messenger of God God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: O Messenger of God, the livestock have perished and the paths have been cut off, so pray to God. So the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed. So it rained from Friday to Friday, and a man came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God! Houses were destroyed, roads were cut off, and livestock were destroyed. He said: “O God, on the tops of the mountains, the hills, and the bottoms of the valleys. And the growths of trees, and they produced a garment for the city.”"
"1795","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Al-Masoudi told us, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Amr bin Hazim, on the authority of Abbad bin Tamim Sufyan said, so I asked Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, he said: I heard it from Abbad bin Tamim, narrating to my father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zaid, The one who was shown the call, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He went out to the prayer place to ask for water, so he faced the Qiblah, turned over his robe, and prayed.” Two rak’ahs.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is a mistake on the part of Ibn Uyaynah, and Abdullah bin Zaid, who was shown the call, is Abdullah bin Zaid bin The servant of his Lord, and this is Abdullah bin Zaid bin Asim (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1796","Muhammad bin Ubaid told us, he said: Hatim bin Ismail, on the authority of Hashim bin Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Kinanah, on the authority of his father, he said: I asked Ibn Abbas about the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, praying for rain, and he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out, rejoicing Humble and supplicant, he sat on the pulpit. He did not deliver this sermon of yours, but he continued to supplicate, supplicate, and glorify God, and prayed. Two rak'ahs as he used to pray on Eid.\ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"1797","Ishaq bin Mansour and Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna informed us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hisham bin Abdullah bin Kinana, on the authority of his father, said: So-and-so sent me to Ibn Abbas, to ask him about the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, for rain rain, and he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out, supplicating, humble, and humble. He did not deliver a sermon like yours, but he prayed two rak’ahs.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1798","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, saying: Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Amara bin Ghaziyah, on the authority of Abbad bin Tamim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zaid, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He asked for rain, wearing a black quilt.”"
"1799","Al-Harith bin Miskin said: It was read to him while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, and Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Abbad bin Tamim told me that he heard his uncle, who was one of the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out One day he was praying for rain, so he turned his back to the people, praying to God, and he faced the Qiblah, and turned his cloak around, then he prayed two rak’ahs.” Ibn Abi Dhib said about the hadith, and he recited in it:"
"1800","Muhammad bin Ubaid bin Muhammad told us, he said: Hatim bin Ismail, on the authority of Hisham bin Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Kinanah, on the authority of His father, he said: I asked Ibn Abbas about the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, praying for rain, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out. And he greeted: “Being humble, humble, and supplicating, he sat on the pulpit, and he did not give this sermon of yours, but he did not cease in supplication and supplication. And the takbeer, and he prayed two rak’ahs as he used to pray on Eid.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1801","Amr bin Uthman bin Saeed bin Kathir told me, he said: Al-Walid, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abid bin Tamim, His uncle told him that: “He went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to draw water, so he changed his cloak and turned his back to the people. He said supplication, then prayed two rak’ahs, and recited aloud.”"
"1802","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of Abbad bin Tamim, on the authority of his uncle: “The Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace: He drew water, prayed two rak’ahs, and turned his cloak over. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1803","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Yahya, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Muhammad, on the authority of Abbad bin Tamim, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Zaid, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He asked for water and turned his cloak over.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1804","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, that he heard Abbad bin Tamim say: I heard Abdullah Ibn Zayd says: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out and drew water and changed his cloak when he faced the Qiblah.”"
"1805","Hisham bin Abdul Malik told us, he said: Na Baqiya, on the authority of Shuaib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abbad bin Tamim, on the authority of his uncle: “It The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw: When seeking rain, he faced the Qiblah, turned the cloak over, and raised his hands."
"1806","Shuaib bin Yusuf told me, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not raise He used his hands to pray for rain, for he used to raise his hands until the whites of his armpits could be seen.”"
"1807","Issa bin Hammad told us, he said: I am Al-Layth, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Sharik bin Abdullah, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, that he heard him say: Between us We were in the mosque on Friday, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was addressing the people. Then a man stood up and said: O Messenger of God, you are interrupted. paths, wealth has perished, and the country has become barren, so pray to God to give us water. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, raised his hands as sandals. His face, and he said: “O God, give us water.” By God, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not come down from the pulpit until we had enough rain, and it rained upon us. That day until the next Friday, then a man got up. I don’t know if he was the one who said: O Messenger of God! Will you draw water for us, or not? He said: O Messenger of God, the paths have been cut off and the property has perished due to the abundance of water, so pray to God to hold back the water for us. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He, peace and blessings be upon him: “O God, surround us, not against us, but rather the mountains and the treetops.” He said: By God, it is only that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, spoke. May God grant him peace. With that, the clouds were torn so that we could not see any of them."
"1808","Humayd bin Masada told us, he said: Yazid bin Zurai’ told us, he said: Sa’id told us, he said: Qatada told us, that Anas bin Malik told them: “That The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not raise his hands in any of his supplications except when praying for rain, for he would raise his hands until white was visible. \His armpits\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""""
"1809","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Khalid bin Yazid, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Hilal, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah, On the authority of Umair, the client of Abu al-Lahm, on the authority of Abu al-Lahm: “He saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, by the oil stones, seeking water. With his hands hooded, he supplicates."
"1810","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Al-Mu`tamir told us, he said: My father told me, he said: Baraka told me, on the authority of Bashir bin Nahik, on the authority of Abu Hurairah said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to raise his hands in supplication until his armpits could be seen.”"
"1811","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Al-Mu’tamir told us, he said: I heard Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He, peace and blessings be upon him, was giving a sermon on Friday, and the people stood up to him, shouted, and said: O Prophet of God, the rain has fallen, and the animals have perished, so pray May God give us water. He said: “O God, give us water.” A cloud, and it spread, then it rained, and the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came down and prayed, then he left, and it did not stop raining until The other Friday, when the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, rose to deliver a sermon, they shouted to him and said: O Prophet of God, the houses were destroyed and cut off. paths, so pray to God to withhold them from us. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, smiled and said: “Oh God, be around us, or against us,” so the The city, and it started to rain around it, and not a drop of it rained in the city, so I looked at the city, and it was like a crown. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1812","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abu Hisham al-Mughirah bin Salamah told me, he said: Wahib told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told me, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O God, give us water.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1813","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Ismail told us, he said: Sharik bin Abdullah told us, on the authority of Anas bin Malik: “A man entered the mosque The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was standing and giving a sermon. He met the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, standing and said: O Messenger of God, you have perished. Money, and the paths were cut off, so pray to God to help us. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, raised his hands and said: “O God, help us. Help us, O God, help us.” Anas said: “By God, we do not see a cloud or a speck in the sky, and there is not a house or a dwelling between us.” He said: Then a cloud appeared like a shield, and when it reached the middle of the sky, it spread out, and then it rained. Anas said: No, by God, we have never seen the sun at night. He said: Then a man entered through that door on the next Friday, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was standing and delivering the sermon, so he met him standing. He said: O Messenger of God! The property has perished and the paths have been cut off, so pray to God to protect it from us. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rose. He extended his hands and said: “O God, protect us, or against us, O God, protect the hills, the valleys, the bottoms of the valleys, and the treetops.” He said: So she took off, and we went out walking in the sun. Sharik said: I asked Anas, is he the first man? He said: No"
"1814","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Muhammad, on the authority of Abbad bin Tamim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zaid, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “went out to draw water, prayed two rak’ahs, and faced the Qiblah.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"1815","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Kinanah, on the authority of his father He said: One of the princes sent me to Ibn Abbas, to ask him about rain, and Ibn Abbas said: What prevented him from asking me, he left. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Humble, humble, humble, and supplicant. He prayed two rak’ahs as he prays on Eid, and he did not propose to you.” This \"" """
